The minimum openable area to the outdoors shall be 5 percent of the floor area of the space being ventilated. Every window or other opening providing required natural ventilation shall be at least 1 foot (304.8 mm) wide and at least 3 square feet (0.28 m

 2 

 ) in total area, providing a minimum of 1 1/2 square feet (0.14 m

 2 

 ) of openable area.

 Exception: Skylights shall comply with the exception of Section 1203.5.1.4.
